WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.317
- So here you are with your first check

00:00:02.317 --> 00:00:05.920
for doing a comedy show.
Look at your little face.

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.753
- Oh!
(audience applause)

00:00:06.753 --> 00:00:08.850
- Your little face with
your braces! I love you.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.766
- Oh my God. Yeah.

00:00:09.766 --> 00:00:14.360
- It's $435.79. So what show was that for?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.450
- It was for my first
television show appearance

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.670
on Comedy Central's show
called "Make Me Laugh".

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.790
And I did the show and
when I got the check,

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.220
I'm like it took me two
minutes to make this.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:26.850
And then in my head, I did the ghetto math

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:27.683
where I'm
- Ghetto math!

00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:28.710
- Ghetto math, where I'm like,

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:29.867
if I did this for eight hours, how much,

00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:32.040
you know, you just start
having those fantasies.

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:32.873
- Yes.

00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:36.520
(audience applause)

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:38.930
- Do you remember the
first thing you bought

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.450
with your first professional money?

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.320
Do you remember?
- That right there.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.780
Yes. And I still have it. A leather jacket

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.160
from Wilson's House of Suede.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:50.220
- I bought a coat. I bought
a coat. I remember that.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.950
- Yeah. It had the liner
with the zipper. Right.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.090
And then it had the thing.
- Oh yes!

00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:56.520
- Oh, it was bad. I still got it.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.390
- [Drew] Fancy.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.272
- Still fits too, what!

00:00:58.272 --> 00:01:02.298
- [Drew] Fancy! I was like,
(audience laughter)

00:01:02.298 --> 00:01:06.100
I was like, literally
remembering and I was like,

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.120
well, that's yester year.
Can't fit into that.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.870
So do you remember your
first acting paid gig though?

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.090
- I was an understudy for a play called

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.480
"Six Degrees of Separation" outta school,

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:19.610
which was a Broadway show. It was amazing.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:22.100
I was the happiest understudy ever,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.890
like most under studies
were sort of like, yeah,

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.080
I'm never going on, but I loved it.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:28.710
I was, I would sit in the catwalk.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.310
I would sit way up high
and watch the show.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:32.730
I loved it to pieces. Yeah.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.840
- I love that. I love those moments too.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.420
Like where I hope I never,
I don't feel like I,

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.910
I still get excited. I hope
I never get jaded like that.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:41.560
You know, you run into
people that get jaded.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.928
- Oh, it's only.
- Yeah.

00:01:43.928 --> 00:01:44.990
- And I don't know where
the accent came from

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:45.880
but that's how I sound when

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.411
I look at mine.
- You go.

00:01:47.411 --> 00:01:48.930
I love that she becomes an old smoker

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:51.427
and you become an old British man.

00:01:51.427 --> 00:01:55.478
- I say, they tried to pay me in Pesos.

00:01:55.478 --> 00:01:58.061
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:00.413
